@startuml sequence-decider-night-sweeps
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: the catalog's own decider calls (issues 190 and 191). A nightly edge
'       sweep types SectionSimilarity pairs into SectionRelation (keyed by the
'       run-independent section keys, so similarity rebuilds keep it); the
'       graph projection draws typed edges and skips hidden pairs. A subject
'       sweep asks two levels of the catalog's own MDT categories and files,
'       queues or skips; librarians accept or reject in the admin.
' Kind: UML sequence diagram, one night, decider reachable. Omitted: auth,
'       failures (a DeciderError ends that night's sweep), MENTIONS/SHOWS.
' Source: EvilFlowersCatalog issues 190, 191 (contract comments, knowledge 64);
'         knowledge Proposals/Decision-Models.md, Diagrams/
'         sequence-decider-graph-sweep.puml (2026-11-16).
' =============================================================================

title Decider night sweeps: typed section pairs and subject suggestions (issues 190, 191, 2026-11-16)

participant "beat → maintenance worker\nevilflowers.catalog.maintenance" as beat
database "postgresql18\nextraction_section_similarity · decider_* ·\nentry_categories · graph library" as db
participant "decider\nPOST /v1/systemone/batch\nmodel = multilingual" as dec
actor "Librarian\nDjango admin" as lib

== decider-edge-sweep (01:00, ≤ 100 min, EVILFLOWERS_DECIDER_EDGE_LIMIT) ==
beat -> db : similar pairs of active runs; untyped first,\nthen typed by another decider_model
db --> beat : section A, section B: summary or first paragraphs
loop ≤ 64 pairs per call
  beat -> dec : choice relation: same · pre · example · loose · none
  dec --> beat : results[] {answers.relation {choice, probabilities}, model}
  beat -> db : SectionRelation(a_key, b_key, relation, p, band, decider_model)\nband = hide for `none` with p ≥ edge.upper
end

== graph-rebuild (04:50) and readers ==
beat -> db : SIMILAR_TO {weight, relation, p, a} unless band = hide;\nSAME_IDEA_AS · PREREQUISITE_OF · EXAMPLE_OF
note right of db : GET /api/v1/sections/{key}/related:\nrelation from the reader's side\n(prerequisite · next · example · general · same · loose), relation_p

== decider-subject-sweep (03:05, ≤ 100 min, EVILFLOWERS_DECIDER_SUBJECT_LIMIT) ==
beat -> db : entries with ≤ 1 MDT subject, not asked by this model
db --> beat : title, abstract, table of contents
beat -> dec : choice category: the catalog's top-level MDT categories
dec --> beat : category, p1
beat -> dec : choice category: its children + "(general)"
dec --> beat : child, p2
alt p1·p2 ≥ subject.upper
  beat -> db : entry.categories.add (never replace);\nSubjectSuggestion status = filed (provenance)
else ≥ subject.lower, or no thresholds yet
  beat -> db : SubjectSuggestion status = pending
  lib -> db : accept (add category) / reject: a labelled case for calibration
else below lower, or already filed
  beat -> db : SubjectSuggestion status = skipped
end
@enduml
